From 682794e14447c9419abe1697d8df1baf156d2c6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yamam <12369962+yamam@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 16:56:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] regression: Restore uim-tutcode conversion after SKK UTF-8
 support (#354)

## Summary

SKK UTF-8 support caused mazegaki conversion in `uim-tutcode` to stop
working. This PR restores the conversion and migrates TUT-Code's
internal string processing to UTF-8.

## Changes

- Add per-file encoding settings for mazegaki and Bushu dictionaries
while retaining EUC-JP defaults.
- Update TUT-Code string handling, dictionary lookup and sorting,
prediction, and input method registration for UTF-8.
- Add Japanese and English migration guides.
- Update gettext extraction lists and Japanese translations.
- Make minor refinements to the SKK migration guides to align their
details with the TUT-Code migration guide.
- Remove the unused SKK setuid state.

---------

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
